 ## Background
-DOF Gaussian Splatting (DOF-GS) was introduced by Yujie Wang, Praneeth Chakravarthula, and Baoquan Chen in a paper titled "DOF-GS: Adjustable Depth-of-Field 3D Gaussian Splatting for Refocusing, Defocus Rendering and Blur Removal" presented at CVPR 2025 [S1, unofficial]. The implementation is primarily based on the official codebase for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) and draws inspiration from Mip-Splatting [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the limitation of standard 3DGS, which renders scenes with a fixed focus determined by the camera's focal plane, by introducing adjustable depth-of-field capabilities.
